# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the setups need
#   to be platform-independent.
#   For an application, you might want to commit this file so that other developers
#   replicate the development environment setup.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#1197, it is "hard recommendation" to commit Pipfile.lock.
#   Guidance for a library or package is opposite: do not commit it.
# Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include poetry.lock in version control.
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include pdm.lock in version control.
# pdm.lock

